		{
			"kind":1,
			"value":"## 10. Conclusion",
			"languageId":"markdown",
			"outputs":[],
			"metadata":{},
			"executionSummary":{}
		},
		{
			"kind":1,
			"value":"A Kalman filter is not simply a smoothing algorithm — it is a **state estimation** algorithm. It uses a model of how the system evolves over time to estimate hidden variables (such as velocity and acceleration) as well as directly observed variables (position).",
			"languageId":"markdown",
			"outputs":[],
			"metadata":{},
			"executionSummary":{}
		},
		{
			"kind":1,
			"value":"That distinction is what makes it so useful in vehicle tracking, robotics, navigation and financial time-series modelling.",
			"languageId":"markdown",
